        "speaker": 7,
        "line": 838,
        "text": "p Sometimes his children, robed in white, stood with him in the chariot, or rode the trace horses... A slave stood behind the conqueror, holding a golden crown and whispering in his ear a warning that all glory is fleeting..."
      }
